created_at":"2026-06-01T01:42:28Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T22:42:30Z","closed_at":"2026-06-02T22:42:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.6.2, 4.6.3\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS\n\n### Issue description\n\nJolt ConeTwistJoint3D appears to be using a pyramid and twist, rather than cone and twist joint. Rapier and Godot Physics behave similarly (cone) and Jolt appears to extend joint freedom into the corners of a pyramid.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBuild a ConeTwistJoint3D and some mechanism to manipulate it. See whether it moves within a cone limited constraint or a pyramid.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTry this scene out with Jolt and then Godot or Rapier Physics and use keys seen in the code to manipulate it. You will see that with Jolt Physics, the cube finds its way further into the corners like a pyramid, while Godot and Rapier behave similarly like a cone. \n\n[cone_twist_joint_3d_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28447808/cone_twist_joint_3d_test.zip)\n\nSorry it's not the perfect test for this issue, but this issue is not a problem for me. I just noticed it when working on Godot-Rapier-Physics and thought the Jolt team would want to know.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.